{"Tool":"WallpaperCost","When":"2026-11-14T01:12:58.0130075+11:00","Machine":"16 logical processors, Microsoft Windows NT 10.0.26200.0","Adapter":"Intel(R) Graphics (video support)","Width":2560,"Height":1440,"Scale":1.25,"SecondsPerRun":15,"Composition":"editorial","Clip":"1920\u00D71080 H.264, 30 fps, 8 Mbit/s, 50 s, no audio track (invented, drawn in code)","Picture":"3840\u00D72160 JPEG (invented)","Caveats":["Offscreen: the layers draw into one bitmap on the GPU. There is no swap chain, no Present, no DWM composition and only one monitor. On the desktop, DWM also composes the surface each frame, and each extra monitor has its own surface.","Paced at 60 fps by a high-resolution timer standing in for vsync, with one frame in flight. A fence stands in for the swap chain\u0027s frame-latency waitable.","Frames are drawn only when the render engine would draw them. With nothing animating (a still picture with nothing playing), the frame clock stops and the run shows almost no frames.","Playing: the app\u0027s controller follows the silent demo player from song time \u224811 s of \u0022Neon Harbour\u0022, with word-timed lyrics and its cover\u0027s colours. The readings are the basic ones, without the Japanese dictionary.","Idle: the controller with no player. This is the app\u0027s \u0022nothing playing\u0022 wallpaper: the default colours, no lyrics, the clock stopped, and the background the settings pick.","Process CPU % is of all cores, from the child\u0027s TotalProcessorTime over the measured window. GPU % is Windows\u0027 GPU Engine counters for the child on the measured adapter, sampled each second.","The tool runs under the JIT, while the app ships as Native AOT. The CPU figures are for JIT-compiled code, and private bytes and working set include the JIT and its metadata, so both read higher than the shipped app\u0027s. Start-up and warm-up are excluded.","Alloc B/frame is the measured window\u0027s render-thread allocations divided by its frames. The note g